To factor the expression \(ab + 5b + 2a + 10\), we can use the method of factoring by grouping.

1. Start with the original expression: \(ab + 5b + 2a + 10\).
2. Group the first two terms and the last two terms: \((ab + 5b) + (2a + 10)\).
3. Factor out the greatest common factor (GCF) from each group:
