Next, we consider the set of all odd numbers greater than zero. The intersection of these two sets will include all numbers that are both prime and odd. Since 2 is the only even prime number, it is excluded from the intersection. The remaining prime numbers (3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23, 29) are all odd and thus included in the intersection.

Counting these elements, we find there are 9 such numbers.

Thus, the number of elements in the intersection is \(\boxed{9}\).
