We set up the equations:
1. \( a_1 + 3d = 200 \)
2. \( a_1 + 7d = 500 \)

Subtracting the first equation from the second:
\[ (a_1 + 7d) - (a_1 + 3d) = 500 - 200 \]
\[ 4d = 300 \]
\[ d = 75 \]

Substituting \( d = 75 \) back into the first equation:
\[ a_1 + 3(75) = 200 \]
\[ a_1 + 225 = 200 \]
\[ a_1 = 200 - 225 \]
\[ a_1 = -25 \]

To find the sixth term:
\[ a_6 = a_1 + 5d \]
\[ a_6 = -25 + 5(75) \]
\[ a_6 = -25 + 375 \]
\[ a_6 = 350 \]

The sixth term is \boxed{350}.
