- \(3a \leq 8\)
- \(3b \leq 4\)
- \(3c \leq 2\)
- \(3d \leq 1\)

Solving these inequalities for \(a\), \(b\), \(c\), and \(d\):
- \(a\) can be 0, 1, or 2 (3 possibilities)
- \(b\) can be 0 or 1 (2 possibilities)
- \(c\) can only be 0 (1 possibility)
- \(d\) can only be 0 (1 possibility)

Thus, the number of possible values of \(x\) is the product of the number of possibilities for each exponent:
\[
3 \times 2 \times 1 \times 1 = 6
\]

