\[ 56 \text{ Drinkets} \times \left( \frac{1 \text{ Blinket}}{\frac{7}{3} \text{ Drinkets}} \right) = 56 \times \frac{3}{7} = 24 \text{ Blinkets} \]

Now, we convert the resulting 24 Blinkets to Trinkets. Since 1 Trinket is equal to 4 Blinkets, we use the conversion factor:

\[ 24 \text{ Blinkets} \times \left( \frac{1 \text{ Trinket}}{4 \text{ Blinkets}} \right) = 6 \text{ Trinkets} \]

Thus, the value of 56 Drinkets in Trinkets is \(\boxed{6}\).
