In permutations, the order matters, so we should use the permutation formula. The formula for permutations when selecting r items from a set of n is nPr = n! / (n - r)!. In this case, n is 10 because there are 10 dishes, and r is 2 because each person is ordering one dish.

So, plugging into the formula, 10P2 = 10! / (10 - 2)! = 10! / 8!. Let's calculate that. 10! is 10 × 9 × 8!, so when we divide by 8!, it cancels out, leaving 10 × 9, which is 90. That's the same result as before.

