To find the remainder when \( f(x) = x^{10} + 5x^9 - 8x^8 + 7x^7 - x^6 - 12x^5 + 4x^4 - 8x^3 + 12x^2 - 5x - 5 \) is divided by \( x^2 - 1 \), we note that the remainder will be a linear polynomial of the form \( ax + b \).

We can use the Remainder Theorem, which states that the remainder of a polynomial \( f(x) \) divided by \( (x - c) \) is \( f(c) \). However, since we are dividing by \( x^2 - 1 \), we use the fact that \( x^2 \equiv 1 \) modulo \( x^2 - 1 \). This allows us to reduce higher powers of \( x \) modulo \( x^2 - 1 \).

We rewrite each term in \( f(x) \) by replacing \( x^2 \) with 1, \( x^3 \) with \( x \), and so on:

- \( x^{10} = (x^2)^5 \equiv 1^5 = 1 \)
- \( 5x^9 = 5(x^2)^4 \cdot x \equiv 5 \cdot 1^4 \cdot x = 5x \)
- \( -8x^8 = -8(x^2)^4 \equiv -8 \cdot 1^4 = -8 \)
- \( 7x^7 = 7(x^2)^3 \cdot x \equiv 7 \cdot 1^3 \cdot x = 7x \)
- \( -x^6 = -(x^2)^3 \equiv -1 \)
- \( -12x^5 = -12(x^2)^2 \cdot x \equiv -12 \cdot 1^2 \cdot x = -12x \)
- \( 4x^4 = 4(x^2)^2 \equiv 4 \cdot 1^2 = 4 \)
- \( -8x^3 = -8(x^2)^1 \cdot x \equiv -8 \cdot 1 \cdot x = -8x \)
- \( 12x^2 = 12(x^2) \equiv 12 \cdot 1 = 12 \)
- \( -5x \) remains as \( -5x \)
- \( -5 \) remains as \( -5 \)

Combining all these terms, we get:

- Constants: \( 1 - 8 - 1 + 4 + 12 - 5 = 3 \)
- \( x \) terms: \( 5x + 7x - 12x - 8x - 5x = -13x \)

Thus, the remainder is \( -13x + 3 \).

The remainder when \( f(x) \) is divided by \( x^2 - 1 \) is \(\boxed{-13x + 3}\). 36%|███▋      | 146/400 [3:53:00<6:55:21, 98.12s/it] 
