\left( \dfrac{37}{8} \right)^{55} \cdot \left( \dfrac{8}{37} \right)^{55}
\]

Next, we recognize that both terms are raised to the 55th power. Using the property of exponents that states \((a/b)^n \cdot (b/a)^n = 1\), we can combine the fractions:

\[
\left( \dfrac{37}{8} \cdot \dfrac{8}{37} \right)^{55}
\]

Simplifying inside the parentheses, we get:

\[
\left( \dfrac{1}{1} \right)^{55} = 1^{55} = 1
\]

