The robot moves at a constant speed and takes 2.5 hours to travel 1 kilometer. To find the speed, we first convert 2.5 hours into seconds:

\[ 2.5 \text{ hours} = 2.5 \times 3600 \text{ seconds} = 9000 \text{ seconds} \]

The speed of the robot is then calculated as:

\[ \text{Speed} = \frac{1000 \text{ meters}}{9000 \text{ seconds}} = \frac{1}{9} \text{ meters per second} \]

Next, we use this speed to find the length of the hallway, which takes 90 seconds to travel:

\[ \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = \frac{1}{9} \text{ m/s} \times 90 \text{ seconds} = 10 \text{ meters} \]

Thus, the length of the hallway is:

\[
\boxed{10}
\]
