The asymptotes of the hyperbola are given as \( y = 2x - 3 \) and \( y = 17 - 2x \). To find the center, we solve for the intersection of these asymptotes:

\[
2x - 3 = 17 - 2x
\]
\[
4x = 20
\]
\[
x = 5
\]

Substituting \( x = 5 \) back into one of the equations to find \( y \):

\[
y = 2(5) - 3 = 7
\]

Thus, the center of the hyperbola is \( (5, 7) \).

