To find all the integer roots of the polynomial equation \(x^4 + 5x^3 + 9x^2 - x - 14 = 0\), we use the Rational Root Theorem, which tells us that any possible rational root is a factor of the constant term divided by a factor of the leading coefficient. The possible integer roots are \(\pm1, \pm2, \pm7, \pm14\).

