\[
\text{Area} = \left| \frac{x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2)}{2} \right|
\]

Plugging in the coordinates (0,0), (2,3), and (10,0):

\[
\text{Area} = \left| \frac{0(3 - 0) + 2(0 - 0) + 10(0 - 3)}{2} \right|
\]

Simplifying the expression:

\[
\text{Area} = \left| \frac{0 + 0 + 10(-3)}{2} \right| = \left| \frac{-30}{2} \right| = \left| -15 \right| = 15
\]

Thus, the area of the shaded triangle is \(\boxed{15}\) square centimeters. 92%|█████████▏| 368/400 [8:52:15<37:44, 70.76s/it] 92%|█████████▏| 369/400 [8:52:51<31:10, 60.35s/it] 92%|█████████▎| 370/400 [8:53:21<25:33, 51.12s/it]
