n - 3 & 3 & n + 1 \\
\hline
n + 2 & 2n - 9 & 1 \\
\hline
2 & n & n - 1 \\
\hline
\end{array}
\]

First, we calculate the sums of the rows:

1. Top row: \( (n - 3) + 3 + (n + 1) = 2n + 1 \)
2. Middle row: \( (n + 2) + (2n - 9) + 1 = 3n - 6 \)
