To determine the probability that the reciprocal of a randomly selected positive odd integer less than 2010 gives a terminating decimal, we need to consider the conditions under which a fraction has a terminating decimal. A fraction \( \frac{1}{n} \) will terminate if and only if \( n \) is of the form \( 2^m \times 5^n \). Since we are dealing with odd integers, \( n \) must be a power of 5.

