2. The distance from the center of the cube to the center of each face is equal to the radius of the sphere, which is 3 inches.
3. Since the distance from the center of the cube to the center of each face is half the edge length of the cube, we have:
   \[
   \frac{s}{2} = 3 \implies s = 6 \text{ inches}
   \]
4. The volume of the cube is calculated as:
   \[
   s^3 = 6^3 = 216 \text{ cubic inches}
   \]

Thus, the volume of the cube is \boxed{216} cubic inches. 97%|█████████▋| 387/400 [9:18:39<20:26, 94.38s/it]  97%|█████████▋| 388/400 [9:19:15<15:22, 76.87s/it]
