- 3 hairstyles + 1 bald = 4 options for hair.
- 2 sets of eyebrows.
- 2 sets of ears.
- 2 sets of lips.
- 2 regular shoes + 1 bonus pair of clown shoes = 3 options for shoes.

The total number of different personalities is calculated by multiplying the number of choices for each required component:

\[
4 \text{ (hair options)} \times 2 \text{ (eyebrow options)} \times 2 \text{ (ear options)} \times 2 \text{ (lip options)} \times 3 \text{ (shoe options)}
\]

Calculating this step-by-step:

\[
4 \times 2 = 8
\]
\[
8 \times 2 = 16
\]
\[
16 \times 2 = 32
\]
\[
32 \times 3 = 96
\]

Thus, the total number of different personalities Tom can create is \(\boxed{96}\). 98%|█████████▊| 392/400 [9:27:57<16:29, 123.65s/it] 98%|█████████▊| 393/400 [9:28:19<10:51, 93.01s/it] 
